details:
(a) whether Government has undertaken or proposes to undertake any assessment or survey relating to domestic workers and the present status thereof;
(b) the existing measures being implemented by Government for the welfare, social security, skill development and protection of domestic workers;
(c) whether a comprehensive policy or legal framework for domestic workers is under consideration; and
(d) the measures taken or proposed to strengthen social security, financial wellbeing and labour protection for domestic workers?

(a) the status of plastic waste generation, collection, processing, recycling and disposal across the country and the steps being taken to strengthen plastic waste management systems;
(b) whether Government is aware of the practice of open burning of plastic waste by residents, particularly in ecologically fragile areas including the Himalayan region and the steps being taken to address it; and
(c) the measures being taken to enforce compliance against open burning of plastic waste and ensure effective implementation of plastic waste management regulations?

(a) the details of clinical trials and research studies undertaken to scientifically validate Ayurvedic medicines and therapies during the last five years;
(b) whether the Ministry has collaborated with national or international research institutions to strengthen evidence-based research in Ayurveda and if so, the details thereof;
(c) the funds allocated and utilised for research and clinical validation of Ayurveda during the last five years; and
(d) the steps taken to promote publication of peer-reviewed research and develop a repository or database of scientifically validated Ayurvedic formulations?

(a) the total length of dedicated urban roads in the country that currently have dedicated, segregated and protected cycling lanes, city-wise and State-wise;
(b) the details of proposals sanctioned or pending approval for creation of dedicated cycling lanes on roads, along with the funds allocated or sought, city-wise and State-wise;
(c) the details of any proposed national policy that mandates dedicated, segregated and protected cycling lanes in all cities across the country; and
(d) the details of any pilot projects in major cities to ensure proper biking lanes for cyclists?

(a) the details of any data or studies available with Government regarding the use of Artificial Intelligence-based platforms by students for mental health guidance, including the extent of such usage and associated risks, if any;
(b) whether any advisory, guideline or cautionary communication has been issued to educational institutions or students regarding reliance on AI-based mental health tools, if so, the details thereof; and
(c) the details of steps taken or proposed by Government to regulate AI-based mental health tools to ensure safeguards for vulnerable users, particularly students?

(a) whether despite regulatory recognition of non-animal testing methods such as organ-on-chip, 3D tissue models and computer-based approaches, India has limited infrastructure for their development and validation and if so, the number of ICMR, CSIR and DBT supported laboratories equipped with such facilities;
(b) whether Government has assessed the impact of limited availability of validated non-animal models on drug discovery, research costs and clinical translation; and
(c) whether Government proposes to strengthen the ecosystem for non-animal testing by establishing validation facilities, promoting indigenous manufacture of related research materials and equipments, and expanding specialised training in this field and if so, the details thereof?

(a) whether Government has assessed the extent of fake, paid or bot-generated product reviews and manipulation of ratings on e-commerce platforms and if so, the findings thereof;
(b) whether any audit or verification mechanism exists or is proposed to detect such manipulation on e-commerce platforms;
(c) whether the Central Consumer Protection Authority (CCPA) has received complaints or initiated action against platforms or sellers for misleading reviews and if so, the details thereof; and
(d) whether Government is considering measures such as algorithmic transparency, disclosure of incentivised reviews and stronger penal provisions to safeguard consumer trust and if so, the details thereof?

(a) whether Government is aware of the incidence of counterfeit and substandard medicines being sold through online platforms and offline channels and if so, Government’s assessment thereof;
(b) the measures taken or proposed to strengthen surveillance, traceability and enforcement against the sale of counterfeit medicines through e-pharmacies and digital marketplaces; and
(c) whether any technology-enabled mechanism has been introduced or is under consideration to enable consumers to verify the authenticity of medicines before purchase and if so, the details thereof?

(a) whether Government is aware of the promotion and sale of e-cigarettes through social media accounts, online platforms and e-stores in contravention of the Prohibition of Electronic Cigarettes Act, 2019 and if so, the action taken thereon;
(b) whether a dedicated enforcement protocol for social media violations under the Act has been issued or is under consideration;
(c) the mechanism in place to address cross-border online promotion of banned e-cigarettes by foreign influencers and international e-stores; and
(d) whether Government has taken steps to check the illegal import of e-cigarettes and if so, the details thereof?

(a) whether Government has taken note of growing public concern regarding the presence of pesticide residues in fruits and vegetables sold in retail markets and their adverse health impact;
(b) whether Government has undertaken any assessment of pesticide residue levels in fruits and vegetables produced in the country, if so, the details thereof;
(c) the steps taken by Government to strengthen awareness among farmers regarding safe and judicious use of pesticides and promote sustainable alternatives through incentives; and
(d) the steps being taken to enhance consumer confidence by improving food safety and quality across the agricultural supply chain?

(a) whether Government has taken note of reports relating to wage kickbacks, illegal wage deductions and underpayment involving contract labourers and the assessment thereof;
(b) whether the existing inspection and grievance redressal mechanisms are considered adequate to address such violations;
(c) whether Government is planning to set up a specific authority and / or helpline to look into such complaints; and
(d) the measures taken or proposed to strengthen enforcement against repeated labour law violations by contractors?

(a) the status of enforcement of the Child Labour (Prohibition and Regulation) Act, 1986 across States/UTs and whether Government has reviewed the effectiveness of rescue operations and conviction outcomes under the Act;
(b) whether shortage of labour inspectors has been assessed as a factor affecting enforcement and rescue operations and the steps being taken to strengthen inspection machinery;
(c) the steps taken to ensure that the rescued children are being provided adequate rehabilitation, education, compensation and reintegration support and the measures in place to prevent re-trafficking; and
(d) the steps taken by Government to strengthen the functioning of Child Welfare Committees across States/UTs?

(a) whether Government has prescribed safety guidelines for schools regarding vehicles used to transport children, including seating capacity and overloading norms;
(b) whether instances of overloading of school vans/buses have come to the notice of Government;
(c) whether Government proposes to take up the matter with State Governments to ensure strict enforcement of safety norms for school transport vehicles, including imposition of penalties on erring vehicles; and
(d) the steps being taken to sensitize schools and transport operators on child safety in commute?

(a) whether Government identifies and monitors accident-prone “black spots” on National Highways across the country;
(b) the criteria and mechanism adopted for identifying such black spots and prioritizing them for rectification;
(c) the steps being taken to accelerate engineering corrections, signage and lighting at such locations to reduce road accident fatalities; and
(d) whether Government proposes to leverage technology, such as AI-based traffic/accident data analysis for early identification of emerging black spots?

(a) whether Government has taken note of the growing challenge of antimicrobial resistance due to inappropriate and non-prescriptive use of antibiotics resulting in their misuse and overuse;
(b) the steps taken to monitor antibiotic consumption and prevent the sale of antibiotics without proper prescription;
(c) whether a national strategy has been implemented to address antimicrobial resistance and strengthen surveillance mechanisms to promote responsible antibiotic use; and
(d) the measures taken to promote awareness and strengthen antimicrobial stewardship among healthcare professionals and the general public regarding the rational use of antibiotics?

(a) whether Government has assessed the proliferation of online astrology and occult-service platforms making unverifiable claims for consideration and the findings thereof;
(b) whether such practices fall within the ambit of misleading advertisements or unfair trade practices under the Consumer Protection Act, 2019 and whether any guidance has been issued in this regard;
(c) whether Government maintains a mechanism for receiving and acting upon consumer complaints relating to such platforms and the details thereof; and
(d) the steps taken or proposed to strengthen consumer safeguards, transparency and regulatory oversight in respect of such platforms?

(a) the details of Urban Local Bodies (ULBs) that have notified bye-laws prescribing spot fines for littering and open dumping under the Solid Waste Management (SWM) Rules, 2016, and those yet to do so;
(b) State-wise data on spot fines levied and collected over the last three years, and its correlation with Garbage Free City ratings and Swachh Survekshan scores;
(c) whether discrepancies exist between ULB-reported Swachhatam Portal data and third-party field assessments; and
(d) whether Government proposes a technology-enabled enforcement framework and intends to increase the quantum of spot fines?

(a) the steps taken by Government to assess the psychological and behavioural impact of excessive social media use on children and adolescents in the country;
(b) whether any age-verification or parental consent mechanisms have been mandated for social media platforms;
(c) the number of complaints received regarding harmful content targeting minors on social media platforms during the last three years, State-wise; and
(d) whether Government proposes to introduce specific safeguards, such as age restricted usage, screen-time alerts or algorithmic transparency requirements, to protect children from addictive design features on these platforms?

(a) whether FSSAI has conducted any national survey on chemical migration from plastic food packaging into food and beverages;
(b) the number of food businesses penalised for non-compliance with migration limits during the last five years, year-wise and State-wise; and
(c) whether India's specific migration limits are periodically benchmarked against EU or Codex Alimentarius standards?

(a) whether Government has undertaken any assessment of urban heat stress in major cities, including the National Capital Territory of Delhi and the key findings thereof;
(b) the details of the measures being taken to incorporate urban heat island mitigation strategies, including cool roofs, enhanced green cover, shaded public spaces and other climate-resilient infrastructure, into urban planning and building frameworks under centrally sponsored schemes; and
(c) whether Government proposes to further strengthen and promote city-level heat resilience plans, including ward-level implementation, to enhance protection for vulnerable groups such as construction workers, street vendors and the details thereof?

(a) whether Government has examined the cost structure and fee components applicable to MSME sellers and small manufacturers on quick commerce platforms such as Blinkit, Zepto and Swiggy Instamart, including commissions, fulfilment charges, storage fees and advertising or visibility-related costs;
(b) whether Government has assessed the impact of such cost structures on the competitiveness, pricing viability and market access of MSMEs participating on such platforms and if so, the details thereof; and
(c) whether Government proposes to take steps to ensure greater transparency in fee structures and fair and equitable digital marketplace access for MSME sellers on quick commerce platforms and if so, the details thereof?

(a) the initiatives taken by Government to promote ward-level citizen participation and institutionalise participatory urban governance through citizen assemblies and other consultative mechanisms;
(b) the status of the constitution and functioning of Ward Committees, wherever applicable, State/Union Territory-wise;
(c) whether the Central Government has evolved any framework to facilitate, monitor and strengthen the functioning of Ward Committees and other participatory bodies in urban local governance, if so, the details thereof; and
(d) the financial, technical and capacity-building support being extended under various central urban development programmes to enhance citizen participation and strengthen ward-level governance, along with the details?

(a) the State-wise details of adventure tourism operators and approved adventure tourism destinations during the last five years;
(b) whether Government has notified uniform national safety standards, certification norms and liability guidelines for adventure tourism activities such as trekking, rafting, paragliding and mountaineering and if so, the details thereof;
(c) the number of accidents, fatalities and safety violations reported in adventure tourism during the last five years, State-wise;
(d) the funds allocated and released for promotion, infrastructure development and capacity building in adventure tourism during those years, year-wise; and
(e) the details of steps taken to ensure insurance coverage, safety audits and trained personnel in the sector?

(a) the total number of calls received on the 181 women helpline no. during the last five years, with year-wise and State-wise/UT-wise details;
(b) the number of cases in which assistance, police intervention, counselling or shelter support was provided, including outcomes of such interventions;
(c) the current staff strength of the helpline compared to sanctioned positions, including counsellors, coordinators and support personnel;
(d) whether Government proposes to enhance ground-level support, including recruitment of additional counsellors, provision of vehicles and expansion of operational capacity; and
(e) if so, the details of such measures, the resources allocated and the proposed timeline for implementation across States and UTs?

(a) the details of surveys conducted under Mission Smile and other schemes during 2023–24 and 2024–25 for identification of persons engaged in begging, State-wise/UT-wise, including the number of areas covered and individuals identified and issued ID cards such as Aadhaar and Ayushman;
(b) the number of persons mobilised and transferred to shelter homes, State-wise, under Mission Smile and other schemes, along with details of new shelters approved, their present operational status and any upgradation of existing shelters;
(c) the number of counselling and de-addiction sessions conducted; and
(d) the number of beneficiaries linked to bank accounts, health services, educational institutions and skill development/livelihood programmes?

(a) the total number of public Electric Vehicle (EV) charging stations sanctioned, installed and operational during the last five years, State-wise and year-wise;
(b) the funds allocated, released and utilised for EV charging infrastructure under various scheme, State-wise;
(c) whether Government has assessed the adequacy of charging infrastructure vis-à-vis registered electric vehicles, if so, the EV-to-charger ratio, State-wise;
(d) the number of charging stations installed in Tier-2 and Tier-3 cities and along national highways, along with the criteria for site selection; and
(e) the roadmap and targets for expansion of EV charging infrastructure over the next three years, including private sector participation?
