(a) total length of urban roads in the country with dedicated, segregated and protected cycling lanes, city-wise and State-wise;
(b) details of proposals received, sanctioned or pending for creating such cycling lanes, along with funds sought, sanctioned and released, city-wise and State-wise;
(c) whether Government maintains data on utilisation and current status of cycling lanes under various urban programmes, if so, the details thereof;
(d) whether Government proposes a national policy or framework mandating dedicated, segregated cycling lanes in all cities and if so, the details and timeline thereof; and
(e) details and outcomes of pilot projects undertaken in major cities to develop or promote dedicated cycling infrastructure?

(a) whether any survey has been conducted in the last five years to enumerate women engaged in home-based, piece-rate textile work, if so, the State-wise number identified;
(b) the number of such workers covered under statutory protections including minimum wages, provident fund and ESI benefits and if data is not maintained, the reasons therefor;
(c) whether Government has assessed occupational health risks, including respiratory illnesses, in recycled textile clusters and the support or compensation provided; and
(d) whether a time-bound framework is proposed to extend formal social security and labour protections to home-based textile workers?
