(a) the number of coal-based thermal power plants in the country over the last five years, State-wise, with installed, operational and idle capacities, year-wise; 
(b) the number of plants with Continuous Emission Monitoring Systems (CEMS) installed, operational, and reporting, with timelines for pending installations; 
(c) instances of exceedance of prescribed emission norms, penalties imposed, collected, or pending, State-wise and year-wise; 
(d) the status of modernisation and efficiency upgrades including supercritical/ultra-supercritical retrofits; and
(e) steps taken to ensure compliance with emission standards and improve monitoring mechanisms?

(a) the total number of war widows and families of martyrs receiving pension under various Armed Forces Pension Rules, category-wise and rank-wise;
(b) the average monthly pension disbursed to war widows and eligible family members, rank-wise, along with the total amount paid annually during the last five years;
(c) the number of beneficiaries who have received ex-gratia or battle casualty compensation during the said period, along with the amount disbursed; and
(d) the details of additional welfare measures extended to war widows and families of martyrs, including housing, medical facilities, educational support for children and employment assistance?

(a) the number of complaints received during last five years relating to catering services - regarding quality, hygiene and pricing of food served on trains and at railway stations, year-wise and zone-wise;
(b) the number of penalties imposed, contracts terminated or contractors blacklisted, including those operating under IRCTC, for violations of quality and safety standards;
(c) whether periodic third-party food safety audits, surprise inspections and laboratory testing of food samples are conducted, if so, the details thereof, year-wise and zone-wise; and
(d) the steps taken to ensure standardisation of pricing, quality control mechanisms and real-time grievance redressal for passengers?

(a) the number of athletes who represented India in recognised international events during the last five years, sport-wise and year-wise;
(b) the number and percentage of athletes currently covered under pension, insurance or post-retirement welfare scheme, scheme-wise;
(c) whether a centralised digital database exists for tracking the post-retirement employment and financial status of former athletes and if so, the details thereof;
(d) whether any nationwide assessment has been conducted during the last five years on economic hardship or mental health concerns among retired sportspersons, including para-athletes; and
(e) whether Government proposes to establish a statutory or contributory National Athlete Welfare Fund and if not, the reasons therefor?

(a) whether Government has worked towards promoting the principle of equal pay for equal work for male and female athletes across various sports disciplines;
(b) if so, the details of remuneration, match fees, prize money, annual contracts, tournament allowance and incentives paid to male, female and trans athletes (including para atheletes) by each National Sports Federation during the last five years, sport-wise and year-wise;
(c) whether any guidelines or advisories have been issued to National Sports Federations to promote gender equity in pay structures and incentives; and
(d) whether financial assistance provided to National Sports Federations is linked to compliance with gender equity norms?

(a) details of vacancies in the posts of Chairpersons and Members of National Commission for Women and State Women’s Commissions, along with year since the vacancy exists;
(b) details of the sanctioned strength, posts filled and vacancies, category-wise and position-wise, Commission-wise, including National Commission for Women (NCW);
(c) number of cases received, disposed of, resolved and pending with NCW and State Women’s Commissions, year-wise and Commission-wise, including number of (suo-motu) cases taken up; and
(d) whether Government has assessed the impact of vacancies, if any, on disposal of cases and overall functioning of these Commissions and steps taken to ensure that vacancies are filled in a time-bound manner?

(a) total number of road accidents, fatalities reported during last five years, with a breakdown by cause, including overspeeding, red-light jumping, other traffic violations, year-wise and State-wise;
(b) whether Government monitors implementation of Good Samaritan/Rah-Veer Scheme to encourage public assistance to accident victims;
(c) State-wise and year-wise number of individuals recognized as Good Samaritans during last five years along with number of persons who have received rewards under old and new incentive structures;
(d) steps taken and funds utilised to raise public awareness about rights, protections and incentives available; and
(e) the average time taken to disburse rewards and measures in place to ensure timely disbursement, State-wise?

(a) the number of packaged food samples found adulterated or non-conforming during inspections by FSSAI and State Food Safety Departments in the last five years commodity-wise, State-wise and year-wise; 
(b) the details of brands and batches recalled during the past five years due to adulteration or contamination; 
(c) the details of import bans, detentions and product rejections of Indian food exports by foreign regulators, commodity, country and quantity-wise, along with the reasons therefor; and
(d) the current status of India’s food testing infrastructure, including laboratories established, upgraded or accredited in the past five years, their capacity, manpower, equipment and operational status?

(a) whether Government has taken cognisance of 2014 Task Force on National Social Assistance Programme (NSAP), which recommended indexing social pensions to inflation, preferably using Dearness Allowance-linked criteria, to protect their real value over time;
(b) whether the task force also recommended uniform minimum pension standards across States with a higher financial contribution from Centre;
(c) if so, action taken by Government on the above recommendations;
(d) if not implemented, the reasons for non-implementation so far; and
(e) whether Government proposes to review or revise the design and financing of NSAP in light of rising inflation and inter-State disparities, if so, the timeline thereof?

(a) whether Government is aware of the increasing demand for rail connectivity to Khatu Shyam Ji from Delhi and nearby areas, if so, the steps taken; 
(b) whether there is any proposal to introduce a direct express train via Rewari-Narnaul-Sikar and to extend existing services like Delhi-Rewari DEMU (74001/74004) and Haridwar-Rewari Express (19617/19620) to Sikar, if so, the status thereof; 
